A '''''Star Wars'' trilogy''' is being written by [[Simon Kinberg]]. It will be the next iteration of the main ''[[Star Wars]]'' films after ''[[Star Wars: Episode IX The Rise of Skywalker]]'', launching a new saga that takes the franchise into the future.

==Development==
{{Quote|He wrote something that we read in August, and it was very good, but not there. We’ve pretty much upended the story, and then spent a great deal of time on the treatment, which he finished literally about four weeks ago. And it’s a very detailed treatment, like 70 pages. And so he is expected to give us something in March.|Kathleen Kennedy|<ref name="Deadline2026">{{WebCite|url=https://deadline.com/2026/01/kathleen-kennedy-exit-interview-1236665253/|text=A Shift In The Force For Lucasfilm’s Kathleen Kennedy: The Exit Interview|author=Mike Flemming Jr.|date=2026-01-15|work=[[Wikipedia:Deadline Hollywood|''Deadline'']]|archivedate=20260115233219}}</ref>}}
[[File:Simonkinberg.jpg|thumb|right|200px|Simon Kinberg will create the next iteration of the ''Star Wars'' franchise.]]
On [[November 7]], [[2024]], [[Wikipedia:Deadline Hollywood|''Deadline'']] reported that [[Simon Kinberg]] will develop and write a new ''[[Star Wars]]'' film trilogy, with [[Lucasfilm]] president [[Kathleen Kennedy]] as a producer.<ref name="Deadline">{{WebCite|url=https://deadline.com/2024/11/star-wars-trilogy-simon-kinberg-movies-1236169916|text=‘Star Wars’ Trilogy Deal: Lucasfilm Taps Simon Kinberg To Write & Produce|author=Mike Fleming Jr|date=2024-11-07|work=[[Wikipedia:Deadline Hollywood|''Deadline'']]|archivedate=20241107171942}}</ref> The [[Wikipedia:The Hollywood Reporter|''The Hollywood Reporter'']] then reported that the films were not a continuation of the [[Star Wars saga|Skywalker Saga]],<ref name="THR">{{WebCite|url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/star-wars-simon-kinberg-trilogy-1236055848|text=‘Star Wars’: Simon Kinberg to Write, Produce New Trilogy for Lucasfilm|work=[[Wikipedia:The Hollywood Reporter|''The Hollywood Reporter'']]|author=Borys Kit|date=2024-11-07|archivedate=20241107212424}}</ref> while ''Deadline'' reported that it would comprise of Episodes X to XII, and would be a new narrative separate from upcoming projects including [[Untitled Star Wars film (Sharmeen Obaid-Chinoy)|the upcoming film]] focusing on [[Rey Skywalker|Rey's]] [[New Jedi Order]] directed by [[Sharmeen Obaid-Chinoy]], [[Untitled Star Wars film (James Mangold)|the upcoming film]] by [[James Mangold]] set in the [[Dawn of the Jedi era]], the [[Untitled Star Wars film (Taika Waititi)|upcoming film]] by [[Taika Waititi]], and the upcoming [[Lando (film)|''Lando'']] film by [[Donald Glover]].<ref name="Deadline" />

On [[February 27]], [[2025]], Kennedy confirmed to ''Deadline'' that Lucasfilm was indeed producing a new ''Star Wars'' trilogy that would start a new saga and the next iteration for the franchise, thus taking it into the future. Development of the trilogy was moving forward expeditiously, and Kinberg had begun going to the script phase of the project and likely deliver a script by June.<ref name="KK Q&A" /> In an interview with Nerdtropolis on [[August 15]], Kinberg cited ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]'' as a source of inspiration.<ref name="Nerd">{{WebCite|url=https://nerdtropolis.com/simon-kinberg-star-wars-trilogy/|text=Simon Kinberg Reflects on Writing and His Upcoming Star Wars Trilogy|work=Nerdtropolis|archivedate=20250821221115}}</ref> On [[August 19]], Kinberg further spoke to [[Wikipedia:ScreenRant|ScreenRant]], stating that he'd find a balance between "big, epic science fiction storytelling with really intimate, dramatic character work." Kinberg further said that {{Film|V}} was one such film that struck that balance, as did ''Andor''.<ref name="ScreenRant">{{WebCite|url=https://screenrant.com/star-wars-trilogy-movies-approach-tease-simon-kinberg/|text=Star Wars' New Trilogy Writer Teases Their Approach For The Next Set Of Movies|work=[[Wikipedia:ScreenRant|''ScreenRant'']]|archivedate=20250826165249}}</ref>

